592186045417] [17592186272038 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272038 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V={R}^{3}$ be the vector space equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+4{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $x=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $y=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186272038 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d09d5e1c-6eb2-558e-9036-de549f8ede79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272038 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $x$ and $y$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+4{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot (-1\\cdot (-2))+4\\cdot (1\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-4+8+4k \\\\  & =4+4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x,y⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4+4k & =0 \\\\ 4k & =-4 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272041 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272041 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140267" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272041 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272041 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V=C[1,e]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[1,e],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{1}^{e}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIf $x(t)={ln}^{2}⁡(t)+k$ and $y(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272041 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d1f86eb4-b13a-5306-8cdf-207f34e53c7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272041 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}({ln}^{2}⁡(t)+k)\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡(t)}{t}+\\frac{k}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡(t)}{3}+k\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}+k & =0 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327046 #edb/ref 1080 "-9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327046 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327046 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0cea311e-0aed-58a9-b41f-6cb7026f351e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327468 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327468 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327468 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3d04ae03-a3a9-5660-9455-6be754d3053c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327560 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327560 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327560 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47e37d21-2b65-5624-8c6f-3a3fcb9d5df1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328222 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328222 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328222 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "938ee061-f1ac-5b53-8f75-1dff5c06744a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328342 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328342 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328342 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a267674c-6c38-552f-85de-adb556b0968b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328470 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328470 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328470 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b0fe3b2c-937b-5969-b4b2-43d693fa584f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328707 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{2}{5}" #edb/ref 1759